## 2. Update the existing API key

You can update an existing API key without generating a new key, provided you authenticate as its owner with the required permissions.

In Kibana Dev Tools:

```

PUT /_security/api_key/<API_KEY_ID>
{
  "role_descriptors": {
    "read-only-role": {
      "cluster": ["monitor"],
      "indices": [
        {
          "names": [
            "logs-kubernetes.container_logs-openshift"
          ],
          "privileges": ["read"],
          "allow_restricted_indices": false
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

```

Important: The update requires the API key owner's credentials and at least `manage_own_api_key`. The key's effective privileges are limited by its owner's permissions.&#x20;

