## 3. Test the permissions

Ask the application team to test using the API key:

```

GET /_cluster/health

GET /logs-kubernetes.container_logs-openshift/_search
{
  "size": 1
}

```

Both should return successful responses when the permissions and index name are correct.

## 4. Response to the application team

The existing API key already provides read access to indices through the wildcard (`*`) configuration.

We can add the Elasticsearch `monitor` cluster privilege to support cluster health checks.

For security best practices, I recommend restricting index access to `logs-kubernetes.container_logs-openshift` if no other indices are required.

Once the API key permissions are updated, please validate both the cluster health endpoint and the index search API.

My recommendation: Add `monitor` at cluster level and restrict index permissions to the required index rather than retaining wildcard access, unless the application genuinely needs to query additional indices.
